# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  PRODUCTION  (www.amigoscloud.com:8444, behind nginx)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Used automatically by:  npm run build
#
# ── Why this is EMPTY, and must stay empty ──
#
# Empty means "the same origin that served this page". Every request becomes a
# relative path — /api/auth/login, /uploads/logo/... — so the browser resolves
# it against whatever address the user actually typed, inheriting the scheme,
# host AND port. nginx proxies those paths to the backend on 127.0.0.1:8585.
#
# Naming the origin here has broken this deployment twice, both times silently:
#
#   https://www.amigoscloud.com:8585   the browser speaks TLS to a port that
#                                      answers plain HTTP → ERR_SSL_PROTOCOL_ERROR
#   https://www.amigoscloud.com        the site is served on :8444, so a call to
#                                      :443 is a DIFFERENT origin → blocked by CORS
#
# Empty is immune to both, and keeps working if the port ever changes.
#
# The code reads this with ?? rather than ||, so an empty string survives
# instead of falling back to localhost — see src/lib/apiClient.js.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

VITE_API_BASE_URL=
